Z||000000||ejayerik||12-25-2001||07:26 PM||||I had the same problem with my Z24. When driving in stop and go traffic or on hot days, after shutting the engine off, it won't start till it cools down. I have replaced the starter in both cars and the whole ignition system and distributor has been replaced in the Fiero. I know the problem sounds like a overheated solenoid but how can this be if I have replaced the starter with a brand new one? It won't even click the starter when I try to start it. After about a half an hour of cooling with the decklid up, it starts right up. I was told by someone about my Z24 that it may be hot rings that are preventing the crank from turning. The car does not overheat. I don't want to be stuck somewhere until the car cools off as I drive the Fiero on a daily basis. Any help?||||reg||4
